# {{ name }} module

A feature module for the [Nreljed platform](https://github.com/nreljed/platform), scaffolded by
`php artisan make:module {{ name }}`.

| Piece           | Value                                          |
| --------------- | ---------------------------------------------- |
| Composer        | `{{ package }}`                                |
| npm             | `{{ npmPackage }}`                             |
| Namespace       | `{{ namespace }}`                              |
| Feature slug    | `{{ slug }}`                                   |
| Routes          | `{{ routePrefix }}` (`{{ routeNamePrefix }}*`) |
| Inertia page    | `{{ pageName }}`                               |
| Permissions     | `{{ slug }}.view`, `{{ slug }}.manage`         |

## Layout

```
src/{{ providerClass }}.php            # identity, routes, nav, permissions
src/Http/Controllers/                  # dashboard controllers
src/Routes/web.php                     # loaded under dashboard/{{ slug }}
src/Resources/js/pages.ts              # {{ pagesFunction }}() page kit
src/Resources/js/Pages/Index.tsx       # the landing page
database/migrations/                   # auto-loaded by the provider
tests/                                 # module test suite
```

## Activate it

`make:module` already wired this module into the app when it was generated with `--activate`.
Otherwise follow the three irreducible steps:

1. **Composer** - register a path repository and require the package:

   ```json
   "repositories": [{ "name": "{{ slug }}-module", "type": "path", "url": "modules/{{ name }}" }],
   "require": { "{{ package }}": "@dev" }
   ```

   ```bash
   composer update {{ package }}
   ```

2. **Feature registry** - add the provider to `config/features.php` and enable it:

   ```php
   'providers' => [ /* ... */ {{ providerClass }}::class ],
   'enabled'   => [ /* ... */ '{{ slug }}' => true ],
   ```

3. **Frontend** - add the npm dependency and spread the page kit into `resources/js/page-config.ts`:

   ```json
   "{{ npmPackage }}": "link:modules/{{ name }}"
   ```

   ```ts
   import { {{ pagesFunction }} } from "{{ npmPackage }}/pages";
   basePages: { ...registerCoreTemplates(), ...{{ pagesFunction }}() }
   ```

   Then `pnpm install` (or `npm install`).

Finally, migrate and sync permissions:

```bash
php artisan migrate
php artisan db:seed --class=RolesAndPermissionsSeeder
php artisan route:list --path={{ routePrefix }}
```

## Growing the module

- **More capabilities**: implement any interface from
  `Nreljed\Platform\Contracts\Capabilities` on the provider - `HasSettings`, `HasDashboardWidgets`,
  `HasAdminResources`, `HasDataBackup`, `HasNotifications`, `HasMedia`, `HasSitemap`,
  `HasHealthChecks`, `HasSharedData`, `HasContentType`, `HasProfileExtension`, `HasDeactivation`.
  No core edits are needed; `FeatureRegistry` dispatches on `instanceof`.
- **Permissions**: declare them in `permissions()` and grant them to roles in `config/roles.php`
  (roles using `'*'` receive new permissions automatically).
- **Frontend**: every `Pages/**/*.tsx` file is picked up by `{{ pagesFunction }}()`; the Inertia
  name is `{{ slug }}/<kebab-cased path>`.
- **Tests**: `vendor/bin/phpunit` in this directory (uses the host app's autoloader).

## Shipping it as a package

This directory is already shaped like a standalone Composer package (`.gitattributes`,
`composer.json`, `package.json`, tests). To publish it:

1. `git init`, commit, and push to `github.com/{{ vendor }}/{{ slug }}-module`.
2. Tag `v{{ version }}` and cut a GitHub Release.
3. In every consuming app, swap the `path` repository for a `vcs` one and require
   `{{ package }}: ^{{ version }}`.
